      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-08T16:46:13.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues exceed analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹124 (up from ₹102 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹121.1b (up 18% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹13.7b (up 22% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 11% (in line with FY 2025). Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 6.1%. Earnings per share (EPS) also surpassed analyst estimates by 85%. Revenue is forecast to grow 6.3% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 14% growth forecast for the Machinery industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 19% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 15% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "2e8f10d2-f097-4847-9b66-4986c9ecf133",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-05-03T12:03:52.000Z",
      "title": "ESCORTS: New Greenfield Capacity Expansion Will Support Future Earnings Re Rating",
      "body": "Analysts have trimmed their fair value estimate for Escorts Kubota from ₹4,642 to about ₹4,510, reflecting updated assumptions for the discount rate, revenue growth, profit margin and future P/E. What's in the News Launch of the Digitrac series under the Powertrac brand, expanding the range from two to five tractor models in the 45–55 HP category for advanced agricultural and heavy haulage applications, available pan India (Product-Related Announcements).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/capital-goods/nse-escorts/escorts-kubota-shares/op5na43b-global-food-demand-and-rural-development-will-spur-agri-mechanization-98lj/updates/4-analysts-have-trimmed-their-fair-value-estimate-for-escorts",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "c171fe40-cbb0-4f1c-8723-c0e1e8498d31",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-04-19T02:08:17.000Z",
      "title": "ESCORTS: Greenfield Expansion Plans Will Restrain Future Return Potential",
      "body": "Analysts have kept their fair value estimate for Escorts Kubota steady at ₹2,828, with updated assumptions indicating higher revenue growth, a slightly lower profit margin, a marginally adjusted future P/E multiple, and a revised discount rate. What's in the News Board meeting scheduled on May 7, 2026 to consider and approve audited financial results for the quarter and financial year ended March 31, 2026 (company filing).",
